    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\tThe drawback in quarduple representation is one extra field required to store the result.<br />\n\tIn triple representation their is no need of extra field to store the result, So it require less space. Both (a) and (b) are correct.</p>"
